course: dictionary
lesson: 2042
title: Finding meaning in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special place or group, and the words around them show you what they mean. «Baptist churches baptise believers by full immersion and let each congregation govern itself.» Here a congregation must be a group of people who belong to one church.
explain: Look at the clue words. Churches are places of worship, and believers are people who have faith, so a congregation is the group of people who worship together. Govern means run, so each congregation runs its own affairs.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Baptist churches let each group of people in the church run itself» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A congregation is the group of people gathered in a church, synagogue or mosque to worship.
fact: A congregation can also mean the members of one particular church or religious community.
fact: «The congregation stood» means the people in the church rose to their feet.
fact: «A large congregation» means many people came to the service.
fact: In a formal sense, a congregation can be any gathering of people or animals, as in «a congregation of birds», though this use is rare.
exercise: «The congregation stood up as the choir walked in.» Who is the congregation? | The choir's music books | The priest's car outside | *The people gathered in the church to worship | The bells in the tower
exercise: «A large congregation filled the church for the wedding.» What does large congregation mean? | *Many people gathered for the service | A very tall building | A loud choir singing alone | A small group of friends at the park
exercise: «A congregation of birds sat on the roof.» What does congregation mean here? | A sleepy bird on a branch | A bird's song | A bird's nest | *A gathering of birds, in a rare, formal way
test: In the sentence «each congregation govern itself», what does congregation mean? | A bishop's robe | *The group of people who belong to one church | A sermon read aloud | A church building
test: Which sentence uses congregation to mean the people in one church? | The congregation was made of wood | The congregation of the building was very tall | The congregation was a lovely shade of blue | *The congregation sang the last hymn together
exam: What is the best meaning of congregation for a pupil? | A minister's sermon | A kind of hymn book | *The group of people gathered in a church to worship | A church building
